WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.060
Workers of the world, unite!

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:04.920
Many people are excited about socialism.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.580
They prefer it to capitalism.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:08.250
So, it’s time for…

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:11.600
A new book, called “The Case Against Socialism”

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.720
You'd think you wouldn't have to write a book

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:15.719
to make the case.

00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:16.880
That's what a lot of people respond.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:18.660
They say, "Oh, the case against socialism?

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:19.750
Wasn't that decided?”

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:21.840
Senator Rand Paul wrote the book because

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.750
for these people, the case obviously isn’t decided.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.620
Don’t they know socialism’s track record?

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:31.280
Hitler's socialism, Stalin's socialism, Mao's socialism.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.600
You would think people would have recognized by now

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:38.160
Paul’s chapter titles highlight socialism’s problems

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.380
It leads to corruption.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.000
It’s a boot stamping on the human face forever

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.130
"Because Eating your Pets is Overrated."

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:47.960
You would think that when your economy gets to the

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:49.760
point where people are eating their pets people might

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:51.300
have second thoughts about what type of

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.920
economic system they’ve chosen.

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:56.800
The eating your pets chapter points out that

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.050
Venezuelans have lost weight because they

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:00.360
cannot find food.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.640
Contrast that with Dear Leader, with Maduro,

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.489
who's probably gained 50 pounds.

00:01:04.489 --> 00:01:07.220
We don’t know that the dictator gained 50 pounds,

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:10.940
but he does eat on TV while his people starve.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:12.880
It really sums up socialism.

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:15.280
There's still a well fed top one percent,

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:17.479
they just happen to be the government or those

00:01:17.479 --> 00:01:19.630
who are cronies or friends of the government.

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:23.060
No Trump, no wall, no USA at all

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.320
American socialists say, we won’t be like that.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:28.320
When I talk about Democratic socialism,

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:30.240
I’m not looking at Venezuela.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.670
I’m not looking at Cuba.

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:34.590
I’m looking at countries like Denmark and Sweden.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.260
They all wind up saying, "Ah, but the kinder,

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:40.770
gentler socialism that we want is Scandinavia.”

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:42.030
That’s the kind of socialism.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:44.360
Democratic socialism in Scandinavia.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:45.860
So we do a big chunk of the book in there

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:47.730
talking about Scandinavia.

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:51.400
Paul’s book is different from other politicians’ books.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.500
Paul did actual research.

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:54.360
It's not true that

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:56.250
the Scandinavian countries are socialist.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:58.440
While Scandinavia tried socialist policies

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:02.230
years ago, they then turned away from socialism.

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:05.860
They privatized industries and repealed regulations.

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:10.000
Denmark is far from a socialist planned economy.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.420
Denmark’s prime minister even came to America

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:14.700
and refuted the socialists’ claims,

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.880
pointing out Denmark is now

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:20.260
A successful market economy with much freedom

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.600
to pursue your dreams and live your life

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:25.860
In fact, when experts rank economic freedom,

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.440
Scandinavian countries rank near the top.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.840
They have private property, private stock exchange.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.640
We learned that, actually,

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:35.680
Bernie is too much of a socialist for Scandinavia.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:38.520
Scandinavia did keep some socialist policies,

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:40.880
like government-run health care.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:43.560
The media say that brings huge benefits.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.080
It’s why Swedes live longer. But...

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.720
This is the trick of statistics.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:49.340
You can say, "Oh, well the Swedes live longer,

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:50.920
and they have socialized medicine."

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:52.600
And yet if you look hard at the statistics,

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:54.900
it started way before socialized medicine.”

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.280
60 years ago, Swedes already lived longer.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:00.720
If you have sauna, you live longer.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:03.480
Likewise, the socialist welfare state

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.110
didn’t reduce poverty.

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:07.040
Scandinavia’s culture did.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.920
For me it’s really, really important to work

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:11.680
Swedes tend to work hard

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:13.580
Paul tells a story about

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:16.400
Nobel prize winning economist, Milton Friedman.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.600
This Swedish economist comes up to him and he says,

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:21.760
"You know in Sweden we have no poverty."

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.000
And Friedman responds and he says,

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.100
"Well, yeah, in America we

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.569
have no poverty among Swedish Americans."

00:03:27.569 --> 00:03:29.840
Today, Swedes in America have a much higher

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:32.870
standard of living than Swedes in Sweden.

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:34.540
Danish Americans too.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:38.440
Socialism simply does not create that magic world of

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:43.659
prosperity plus equality that today’s socialists suggest.

00:03:43.659 --> 00:03:45.340
But the biggest case against it

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:47.140
is that it crushes freedom.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:52.140
Socialists get elected by promising fairness

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:53.150
and equality.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:54.340
The only way you can enforce those things

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:56.750
is you have to have an equality police or

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:57.340
a fairness police,

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:59.360
and ultimately they show up with truncheons.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.740
Tanks, tear gas, and riot police

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:03.900
Why does it always lead to

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:07.290
“a boot stamping on your face forever?”

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:08.760
If you want complete socialism,

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.010
you have to take the property from people.

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:15.000
Here’s Hugo Chavez doing that.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.759
The best kind of socialist leader ends up

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.460
having to be ruthless because you can't be

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:26.220
a kinder, gentler socialist leader

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:27.460
and get the property.

00:04:27.469 --> 00:04:28.879
So many choices!

00:04:28.879 --> 00:04:32.340
By contrast, capitalism largely lets individuals

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:34.389
make our own choices.

00:04:34.389 --> 00:04:36.689
It's a direct democracy every day.

00:04:36.689 --> 00:04:37.960
You vote either for Walmart,

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.449
or you vote for Target.

00:04:39.449 --> 00:04:41.639
You vote with your feet, with your wallet.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.060
And the people who succeed are the people

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:45.640
who get the most votes, which are dollars.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:47.460
And as long as there's no coercion,

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:50.600
seems to me that that would be the most just way

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.900
of distributing a nation's economy

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.800
At your service!

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:57.740
It’s good that Senator Paul is around to tell his fellow

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:00.680
politicians the truth about socialism:

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:01.940
It doesn’t work.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:03.980
It’s a recipe for disaster.

00:05:03.980 --> 00:05:06.120
Look what happens as we approach socialism

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:06.999
around the world.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:10.380
It’s a history of famine and genocide.

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:12.180
When working families are under attack

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:13.260
what do we do?

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:15.880
Stalin, Hitler, Mao,

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:19.900
Pol Pot, Castro, Chavez, Maduro.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.900
It doesn’t work.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.160
Hope you enjoyed this video.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:26.880
Please click that button to help us make more.

